        "original_id": "898bffba-57ed-5e10-97a4-c03b0760722d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Buildings: Marine Midland Building, 4 World Trade Center\n- Places: New York City, World Trade Center site\n- Artworks: Isamu Noguchi's \"Cube\"\n\nFacts:\n- The Marine Midland Building was completed in 1967.\n- The Marine Midland Building is 688 feet (209.7 meters) tall.\n- The Marine Midland Building is known for the sculpture at its entrance, Isamu Noguchi's \"Cube.\"\n- 4 World Trade Center, also known as 150 Greenwich Street, is a skyscraper in the World Trade Center complex in New York City.\n- 4 World Trade Center is located on the southeast corner of the 16-acre World Trade Center site, where the original nine-story 4 World Trade Center once stood.\n- As of 2016, 4 World Trade Center was the third tallest skyscraper at the rebuilt World Trade Center, behind One World Trade Center and 3 World Trade Center.",
